n Sunday.\"Compute campuses better describes the scale and role of the infrastructure we're building for AI,\" the spokesperson said. \"These are long-term investments in computing, energy infrastructure and skilled work.\"Though much has been said about the less-than-stellar reputations of AI data centers (a recent Pew Research poll found that 54% of Americans say AI data centers are bad for the environment), efforts to ameliorate that view have mostly failed. Data centers are now a major issue for voters in the midterms.While major data center builders like Meta, Amazon, and Microsoft have pledged millions of dollars to the communities and schools surrounding their centers, OpenAI is betting that a complete rebrand will also help turn around public opinion.\"We want the communities hosting that infrastructure to help shape it and share in the opportunities it creates,\" the OpenAI spokesperson said.Time will tell, however, if the \"compute campus\" lingo catches on.Axios earlier reported that OpenAI was also preparing for a blue wave in Tuesday's midterm elections, which could result in a more regulatory-minded government. Read next Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Truman Dickerson You're currently following this author! Click to unsubscribe from email alerts. Truman Dickerson is the Weekend News Fellow at Business Insider, based in New York City. He covers trending tech and business news. He previously reported for The Boston Globe's Express Desk. He graduated from Boston University, where he served as editor in chief of The Daily Free Press, BU's student-run newspaper.Contact him at Tdickerson@insider.com OpenAI Data Centers Sam Altman More ChatGPT","fetched_at":"2026-11-02T22:21:52.850Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><span>By</span>\n       